# Linux Logging for SOC: Incident Triage & Runtime Telemetry

##  Project Overview
This repository contains my write-up, technical analysis, and investigative workflows compiled while completing the **Linux Logging 
for SOC** room on TryHackMe. The core objective of this project was to master the navigation of chaotic Linux logging structures,
isolate security incidents out of noisy plain-text files, and reconstruct adversary footprints using advanced runtime auditing frameworks
(`auditd`).

##  Core Tools & Technologies
*   **Log Frameworks:** Linux Syslog (`/var/log/syslog`), Authentication Logs (`/var/log/auth.log`), Package Management
Logs (`/var/log/dpkg.log`)
*   **Auditing Frameworks:** Linux Audit Daemon (`auditd`), Runtime Telemetry Parser (`ausearch`)
*   **Analysis Tools:** Command-Line Utilities (`grep`, `cat`, `pipes`, `strings`)

